# playpick cell: mode=clear spec=hunter:marksmanship style=auto size=25
# difficulty=heroic view=820x1180,touch save=carried (behaves as fresh, #273 --
# carried never actually carries across separate playbot invocations because
# the dev-server port is derived from the process pid).
#
# A fresh/carried save only opens Bonegrinder 10-normal by default, so
# #b=marrow&s=25&h=1 unlocks the whole chain up to 25-heroic before backing
# out to a real RAID -> WALK IN at the door (direction.md's 2026-09-26
# driver-lesson recipe), rather than landing on the invite's own single-fight
# "visiting" framing.
#
# What no session has done before: direction.md's #6/auto driver-lesson note
# says auto never sets a steering vector at all (scripts/playbot.ts) -- every
# prior auto reading confirming that was a caster dps, two healers, or a
# melee dps (rogue:assassination, the one prior auto+clear+25-heroic evening,
# 2026-09-28-17.play). None of those was a ranged class that starts a fight
# already within its own attack range without needing to close distance --
# hunter:marksmanship is the roster's other pure ranged dps alongside the
# warlock/mage/shaman casters already read this way, but no auto reading has
# been taken on it, and none has asked whether "never moves" costs a ranged
# body less than it costs a melee one when the pull's own opening position is
# already in range. This is also the first hunter:marksmanship evening this
# job has run under mode=clear at all (its four priors were all mode=walk
# coverage-label single-corridor runs under `flee`), and the first auto+clear
# reading at this viewport (820x1180,touch; the one prior was 844x390).
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
tap next
tap class:hunter:marksmanship
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start

